        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve(matrix): prove lifecycle parity across substrates",
        "body": "Closes #101054\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nMatrix transport tests need one lifecycle contract for cold start, idempotent start, restart, stop, and resume so the same behavioral scenarios can run against both the Docker-backed Tuwunel live driver and Crabline's Matrix channel driver.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe architecture follows the existing selected-driver boundary and remains test-only:\n\n1. `lifecycle.test-support.ts` owns only substrate-neutral state transitions and assertions. It knows that a runtime has a `baseUrl`, but knows nothing about Tuwunel or Crabline.\n2. `tuwunel-lifecycle.test-support.ts` wraps the existing Matrix live-driver harness and preserves its resolved port across restart/resume. Its Docker proof is a `.live.test.ts` lane, so intentional live-test selection controls provisioning.\n3. Crabline lifecycle proof lives beside `crabline-transport.ts` in QA Lab. It selects `{ channel: \"matrix\", channelDriver: \"crabline\" }` and starts through `createQaCrablineTransportAdapter`; the Matrix plugin contains no Crabline-specific implementation or policy.\n4. `test-api.ts` is a private test surface. It is excluded from bundled plugin build entries, so the lifecycle helpers do not enter the Matrix runtime bundle.\n\nThe lifecycle contract permits a substrate to return a new endpoint after restart while proving the replaced endpoint is no longer reachable. The same five scenarios and Matrix differential probe run against both selected driver lanes.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo end-user Matrix runtime behavior, configuration, environment-variable surface, public package contents, or runtime bundle size changes. Maintainers gain executable lifecycle parity proof without duplicating Crabline transport ownership or introducing QA-named lifecycle concepts into the Matrix plugin.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact pushed head: `f55aaa96a365f38eb51403bb247ee9434ac85fd2`.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kwwgyv67zt51fpc6hkehgyzm`:\n  - `node scripts/test-live.mjs -- extensions/qa-matrix/src/substrate/lifecycle.live.test.ts` passed all five Tuwunel lifecycle scenarios.\n  - `pnpm test extensions/qa-lab/src/crabline-transport.lifecycle.e2e.test.ts extensions/qa-matrix/src/substrate/lifecycle.test.ts` passed the adapter-owned Crabline five-scenario proof and three shared controller tests.\n  - `pnpm check:changed` passed production/test typechecks, extension lint, dependency/package guards, database-first guard, runtime sidecar guard, and import-cycle checks.\n- Guard warning proof: `node scripts/report-test-temp-creations.mjs` reports no new temp-directory migration warnings on this head.\n- Bundle proof: the qa-matrix build graph contains only `index`, `cli`, and `runtime-api`; the lifecycle test support contributes 0 runtime entries. qa-matrix also has no public package artifacts.\n- Production boundary check: the Matrix plugin has no Crabline lifecycle implementation; Crabline-specific setup is confined to the Crabline transport adapter test.\n- Direct upstream contract inspection: Crabline `0.1.9` owns `startOpenClawCrablineAdapter`, Matrix provider probing, Matrix manifest/config translation, and adapter-owned inbound injection.\n- Fresh autoreview thread `019f3914-9f0f-7c03-b921-561c56f18d26` completed with no accepted or actionable findings after preserving lifecycle body failures through Tuwunel cleanup.\n\nDeveloped with AI assistance. A sanitized agent transcript is available but is not included without explicit approval.\n",
